          "start": 4602,
          "end": 4989,
          "text": "EHA Research Grants are designed to support the future of hematology by helping talented junior researchers to:\nConduct basic or translational lab-based research\nGain valuable research and leadership experience\nMove towards becoming group leaders\nAdvance their careers\nYou’re eligible if:\nYou’re an EHA member\nYour institute is an academic research center or proven equivalent in Europe\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s46",
          "doc_id": "web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec",
          "start": 4226,
          "end": 4602,
          "text": "EHA Research Grant review and selection process\nExtending the reach of EHA Grants\nWhat an EHA Research Grant covers\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\nEHA Innovation Grant\nEHA Kick-off Grant\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\nEHA Travel Grants\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\nScope of our grants\nThe call has closed. Winners will be announced by mid-April 2027.\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s48",
          "doc_id": "web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec",
          "start": 4989,
          "end": 5372,
          "text": "You have the support of an academic department and institute\nYour application relates to basic and translational lab-based research in hematology\nYour application will not be eligible if it relates to:\nPurely clinical research projects\nProjects in health economics\nOther non-lab-based research\nHowever, it may be eligible if it relates to the translational part of a clinical trial. ",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s49",
          "doc_id": "web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec",
          "start": 5372,
          "end": 5741,
          "text": "In this case, it must be both relevant and novel.\nTypes of EHA Research Grants\nThe three types of EHA Research Grant are the:\nEHA Junior Research Grant, which can provide up to €150,000 for three years\nEHA Advanced Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years\nEHA Physician Scientist Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s50",
          "doc_id": "web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec",
          "start": 5741,
          "end": 6073,
          "text": "Each one of the three types of EHA Research Grant also has its own specific eligibility criteria. Please make sure you read the eligibility criteria for your grant type before you apply.\nTopics-in-Focus Research Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. ",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s51",
          "doc_id": "web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec",
          "start": 6073,
          "end": 6453,
          "text": "Please select the ‘Topics-in-Focus Research Grant’ version of your grant type on your application form.\nExtending the reach of our grants: If you are operating in a country less-represented among EHA grantees, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. ​You can see a full list of these countries on our page about extending the reach of EHA Research Grants.\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
