        {
          "id": "s230",
          "doc_id": "web-5ea6489c02f2281589b4de8a",
          "start": 6019,
          "end": 6374,
          "text": "The track record and international standing of the investigator.\nThe skills and expertise of the investigator (and collaborators, if applicable).\nThe commitment to research culture and extramural activities.\nBudget considerations\nAre the budgeted activities clearly listed and assigned?\nAre the costs of resources/activities researched and substantiated?\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s231",
          "doc_id": "web-5ea6489c02f2281589b4de8a",
          "start": 6374,
          "end": 6756,
          "text": "Can the project be achieved with the resources and planned timeline?\nOverall evaluation\nTo what extent does the proposed research address important challenges?\nTo what extent are the objectives ambitious and beyond the state of the art (e.g. novel concepts and approaches)?\nTo what extent is the proposed research high risk/high gain?\nWhat happens at the end of the external review\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s232",
          "doc_id": "web-5ea6489c02f2281589b4de8a",
          "start": 6756,
          "end": 7074,
          "text": "This external review will produce feedback both for the Fellowships and Grants Committee and for you as the applicant. The Committee will use this feedback to decide who to invite for an interview.\nWhatever the outcome of your application, you’ll receive the external review feedback after the awardees are announced. ",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s233",
          "doc_id": "web-5ea6489c02f2281589b4de8a",
          "start": 7074,
          "end": 7289,
          "text": "We hope that this feedback will provide some guidance on how the application and research plan could be improved. Please note that there will be no further correspondence regarding this feedback.\nStep 4: Interviews\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s234",
          "doc_id": "web-5ea6489c02f2281589b4de8a",
          "start": 7289,
          "end": 7676,
          "text": "Successful applicants will be invited to a video interview (max 25 minutes) where they will be given the opportunity to present their proposal (max 10 minutes) and answer questions (max 15 minutes) on it.\nThese interviews are scheduled for April 7-9, 2027.\nActions after a grant has been awarded\nStarting your project\nYou must start your project within one year of receiving your award.\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s235",
          "doc_id": "web-5ea6489c02f2281589b4de8a",
          "start": 7676,
          "end": 8076,
          "text": "Grant agreement\nYou must provide all of necessary information for the funding agreement. This will include:\nBank details\nThe project’s start date\nYou and your institute must also sign the grant agreement, which all parties read and approved during the application phase, within 90 days of receiving the award.\nIf you withhold this approval, you may become ineligible and your award may be withdrawn.\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s236",
          "doc_id": "web-5ea6489c02f2281589b4de8a",
          "start": 8076,
          "end": 8410,
          "text": "Your obligations\nOnce the grant agreement has been signed, the first installment is transferred to your institutes according to the disbursement schedule in the agreement.\nInterim reports\nWe expect to receive interim scientific and financial reports halfway through the project. You’ll receive templates for these reports in advance. ",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s237",
          "doc_id": "web-5ea6489c02f2281589b4de8a",
          "start": 8410,
          "end": 8802,
          "text": "Your second installment will be paid once your interim reports are approved.\nFinal reports\nWe expect to receive your final scientific and financial reports within six weeks of your project’s end date. Your final financial report must be audited and signed off by an external auditor and the institute’s financial head. Your last installment will be paid once your final reports are approved.\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s238",
          "doc_id": "web-5ea6489c02f2281589b4de8a",
          "start": 8802,
          "end": 9139,
          "text": "The Fellowships and Grants Committee is responsible for reviewing all scientific reports.\nPublications\nAny publication arising from work funded by EHA must acknowledge EHA funding, as stated in the grant agreement.\nAmendments\nAny deviations from the approved project scope or budget must be formally requested before you implement them. ",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s239",
          "doc_id": "web-5ea6489c02f2281589b4de8a",
          "start": 9139,
          "end": 9525,
          "text": "For guidance on this, please email the EHA Grants Manager at [email protected].\nTracking your grant’s impact\nAs an EHA award winner, we want to hear more about:\nHow the award has helped you\nThe impact it’s had on different aspects of your work, from collaborations to publications, or even additional funding\nThis is why we work with Researchfish to track research and evidence impact.\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s240",
          "doc_id": "web-5ea6489c02f2281589b4de8a",
          "start": 9525,
          "end": 9924,
          "text": "Submissions via Researchfish are mandatory during the grant period and for up to five (5) years following the end of the Grant, and thereafter upon EHA’s request.\nEvery January, you’ll receive an email with details about the status of your submission.\nShare\nEHA Research Grants\nHow to apply for an EHA Research Grant\nEHA Research Grant review and selection process\nExtending the reach of EHA Grants\n",
