          "start": 4259,
          "end": 4621,
          "text": "EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\nEHA Innovation Grant\nEHA Kick-off Grant\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\nEHA Travel Grants\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\nScope of our grants\nThe EHA Advanced Research Grant is a type of EHA Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years.\nEligibility\nYou’re eligible if:\nYou’re an EHA member\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s284",
          "doc_id": "web-0bba10627d55bbfd09470f5c",
          "start": 4992,
          "end": 5329,
          "text": "However, it may be eligible if it relates to the translational part of a clinical trial. In this case, it must be both relevant and novel.\nSpecific criteria for the EHA Advanced Research Grant\nOur Advanced Research Grant is suitable for researchers who:\nAre currently carrying out basic or translational lab-based research in hematology\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s285",
          "doc_id": "web-0bba10627d55bbfd09470f5c",
          "start": 5329,
          "end": 5641,
          "text": "Received a PhD or PharmD less than eight years before the closing date listed above\nHave at least one first author publication\nIf you received your PhD or PharmD outside of this timeframe, please check our policy on life events. If this policy applies to you, you can ask us to extend the period of eligibility.\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s286",
          "doc_id": "web-0bba10627d55bbfd09470f5c",
          "start": 5641,
          "end": 5872,
          "text": "Topics-in-Focus Research Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. Please select the ‘Topics-in-Focus Advanced Research Grant’ on your application form.\n",
          "source_role": "document",
          "source_message_indices": [],
          "time_metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s287",
          "doc_id": "web-0bba10627d55bbfd09470f5c",
          "start": 5872,
          "end": 6259,
          "text": "Extending the reach of our grants: If you are operating in countries less-represented among EHA grantees, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. ​You can see a full list of these countries on our page about extending the reach of EHA Research Grants. Applicants, who received their PhD or PharmD more than eight years before the closing date, are also eligible.\n",
